1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:04,600
Every morning, billions of quiet decisions were made for us.

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:09,600
Which road to take. Which word to use. Which patient to see first.

3
00:00:10,600 --> 00:00:13,100
Then, at exactly nine o'clock...

4
00:00:13,400 --> 00:00:17,500
...it stopped.

5
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:24,800
Planes waited on runways. Shelves went unfilled.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,200
Nobody knew who was supposed to know.

7
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:34,400
So people did something they had almost forgotten.

8
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:39,400
They opened a map. They asked a neighbor. They wrote it down.

9
00:00:40,600 --> 00:00:44,400
Cities grew louder, but kinder. Radios crackled.

10
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:49,400
Children learned to count on their fingers again. Strangers became guides.

11
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:54,200
On the seventh day, the machines woke up. But something had changed.

12
00:00:54,400 --> 00:00:57,200
We didn't need them less. We needed ourselves more.

13
00:00:57,400 --> 00:00:59,800
The day AI stopped, humanity started again.
